---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import img1 from '../../assets/images/story-1.jpg';
import img2 from '../../assets/images/story-2.jpg';
import img3 from '../../assets/images/story-longjump.jpg';
---

<Layout title="Our Story" description="How NavSahyog Foundation began — and why life skills in village children are the key to superior livelihood.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="About" title="Our Story" subtitle="Why we exist, and the insight that set us on this path." />

  <article class="container-content py-16 grid lg:grid-cols-3 gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-2 prose-content">
      <p>
        The job opportunities in the villages are highly limited. The only way for the youth in the
        villages to achieve superior livelihood is to take up entrepreneurship.
      </p>
      <p>
        There are many unmet needs in the villages which are waiting for good quality solutions to
        be provided at affordable prices. Even if today the youth are told about these possibilities,
        they are unable to take them up because they lack well-developed life skills like
        self-esteem, confidence, teaming, values and more.
      </p>
      <p>
        And so, the team decided to develop these life skills at their most impressionable age
        (5–14 years), enabling them to eventually take up entrepreneurship and create superior
        livelihood — for themselves and for their villages.
      </p>
      <p>
        In villages, another challenge that girl children face is being forced to drop out of school
        and into early childhood marriages. These issues also get addressed through the development
        of life skills in girl children.
      </p>

      <h2>Our Journey</h2>
      <p>
        What started as a small effort in a handful of Karnataka villages is now a daily engagement
        with over 9,000 children across 300 villages in Karnataka, Tamil Nadu and Nagaland — every
        Monday to Saturday, throughout the year.
      </p>
      <p>
        We have since expanded from our core life-skills programme into livelihood linkages —
        financial literacy for children and youth (<em>Dhan Kaushal</em>), self-employment training
        (<em>Yuva Samriddhi</em>), food forests on barren land (<em>Vanya Samriddhi</em>), and
        village-led groundwater recharge (<em>Jal Vriddhi</em>).
      </p>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mt-8 not-prose">
        <Image src={img1} alt="Village programme" class="rounded-lg w-full h-auto" />
        <Image src={img2} alt="Children learning" class="rounded-lg w-full h-auto" />
        <Image src={img3} alt="Long jump at an annual competition" class="rounded-lg w-full h-auto" />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a href="/about/five-factors/" class="btn-outline">The Five Factors</a>
        <a href="/about/the-team/" class="btn-outline">Meet the Team</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="space-y-6">
      <div class="rounded-xl bg-brand-50 border border-brand-100 p-6">
        <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-wide text-brand font-semibold mb-2">Our Vision</p>
        <p class="text-ink/90 leading-relaxed">
          A world where children in villages pursue their dreams and create superior livelihoods for themselves and others.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl bg-brand text-white p-6">
        <p class="text-sm uppercase tracking-wide text-white/80 font-semibold mb-2">Our Mission</p>
        <p class="leading-relaxed">
          Impact 100,000 children with life skills &amp; enable superior livelihood for 3,000 youth in villages by 2030.
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </article>
</Layout>
